{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/287287-help-finding-games-in-pa-or-nj","id":287287,"title":"Help finding games in PA or NJ","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-19T23:28:50-07:00","id":287287,"title":"Help finding games in PA or NJ","content":"Does anyone have any leads on WOD tabletop games in PA or NJ (the closer to philly the better but I would travel anywhere within a couple of hours). I have had absolutely no luck looking online and inquiring at local game stores. If others in the area are also looking for a game, please get in touch. I own a great deal of WOD books from various systems. I prefer old WOD and 20th anniversary products. I would play or run any of them. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3344-thelongnight","name":"TheLongNight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3344_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T00:13:59-07:00","id":287321,"title":"","content":"Having grown up in the Philly area of the world, most of the people I know that are playing WOD games are still kind of pretty close knit groups. I know a LARP group in Newark DE (which you can get to from SEPTA train, so you're not completely SOL on distance) that's actively recruiting (mostly because a friend of mine tries to drag me out for events once and awhile). They have some smaller TT groups within the larger one and mostly do VtM and WtA.<br /> <br /> Outside of that I'm not super comfortable with too much else because, well, they're personal friends and we're two people that know almost nothing about each other. Sorry to be a bit blunt on that, but I hope you can understand the hesitation. When I get a chance to talk to people next time I'm back in the area, I'll see if anyone's comfortable coming here and dropping you a line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T11:42:35-07:00","id":288716,"title":"","content":"Oh I certainly understand, I would not send an anonymous online player to a friend without some vetting first. If anyone does happen to be looking for players I am always happy to field emails and see if I might fit. I have met folks from local LARPs who are very friendly and helpful, but I have not found myself to be a huge fan of LARP compared to tabletop play. I have no problem finding groups of people for other RPGs but I have left area where I knew lots of people that played WOD. As you say, often close knit groups. Thanks for the reply. Much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3344-thelongnight","name":"TheLongNight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3344_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}